\\"; icons present are only lucide-users, lucide-chevron-down, lucide-trash2, lucide-plus.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Empty submit: blocked, focus moved to #name, native message \\\"Please fill out this field.\\\". Invalid email \\\"alex-at-example\\\": blocked, focus moved to #email, native message \\\"Please include an '@' in the email address...\\\". Name/email/message are required; phone is optional (required=false). No application was created in either case.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing job-posting validation: invalid salary range and empty skills accepted\", \"actual\": \"Submitted \\\"QA Automation Engineer\\\" with min salary 200000 > max salary 100000 and ZERO required skills. The job was published successfully (toast \\\"Job posted successfully!\\\") and appears in the dashboard as \\\"$200k - $100k\\\". No validation feedback was shown. Additionally, submitting a completely empty form produced no error message or field-level feedback at all (form silently did nothing).\", \"evidence\": \"Dashboard entry: \\\"QA Automation Engineer / Austin, TX · $200k - $100k · Posted Yesterday\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No duplicate-email guard on job applications\", \"actual\": \"After successfully applying to job-1 as alex.rivera@example.com, a second application was submitted for the SAME job with the same email (\\\"Alex R Duplicate\\\"). It was accepted with the same success toast \\\"Application submitted!\\\". The employer dashboard now shows \\\"Applications (4)\\\" for Senior Frontend Developer containing two separate records both with alex.rivera@example.com. No error or warning was shown.\", \"evidence\": \"Dashboard applications list: \\\"Alex R Duplicate / alex.rivera@example.com\\\" and \\\"Alex Rivera / alex.rivera@example.com / 555-0199\\\" under the same job. Job application count rose 3 -> 4.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submission showed toast \\\"Application submitted! Your application for Senior Frontend Developer at TechCorp Solutions has been sent.\\\" The \\\"Alex Rivera\\\" record appears exactly once under Senior Frontend Developer in the employer dashboard with the exact submitted name, email, phone and message.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each search keystroke/filter selection instantly updates cards and \\\"Showing N jobs\\\". Search \\\"zzzznotexist\\\" -> \\\"Showing 0 jobs\\\" plus \\\"No jobs found / Try adjusting your filters or search terms\\\" empty state. Clear filters restores 9 jobs and empties the search box.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all state is in-memory and resets on page reload\", \"actual\": \"Before reload: 8 seeker jobs incl. newly published \\\"QA Automation Engineer\\\", \\\"Product Designer\\\" deleted, Senior Frontend Developer with 4 applications (2 newly submitted), dashboard 5 active / 4 applications. After reloading http://localhost:6003/: the published job \\\"QA Automation Engineer\\\" is GONE, the deleted \\\"Product Designer\\\" is BACK, and the dashboard resets to 5 active jobs / 3 applications with Senior Frontend Developer back to 2 applications — losing both new applications. localStorage/sessionStorage are empty, confirming no persistence layer.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-reload listing titles: Senior Frontend Developer, Product Designer, Registered Nurse, Marketing Manager, Data Analyst, Part-Time Content Writer, DevOps Engineer (Contract), Elementary School Teacher — identical to the original seed set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each card shows industry (Technology), type (Full-time), title (Senior Frontend Developer), company (TechCorp Solutions), location (San Francisco, CA), salary ($140k - $180k), date (Jan 15), skills (React, TypeScript, CSS, Node.js)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/jobs/job-1 shows Technology, Full-time, \\\"Senior Frontend Developer\\\", TechCorp Solutions, San Francisco CA, $140k - $180k, \\\"Posted Jan 15\\\", full description with Responsibilities/Requirements sections, and skills React/TypeScript/CSS/Node.js — all matching the listing card.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each application renders as a distinct card: \\\"Alex Rivera / alex.rivera@example.com / 555-0199 / Yesterday / I have 6 years of React experience...\\\". Optional phone is simply omitted when not supplied (Alex R Duplicate). Seeded records show name/email/phone/date/message likewise.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Off-by-one relative date: items created today are labelled \\\"Yesterday\\\"\", \"actual\": \"Browser clock is Fri Aug 28 2026 08:03 UTC. The job posted moments earlier displays \\\"Posted Yesterday\\\" in the employer dashboard and \\\"Yesterday\\\" on its job-seeker card. Both applications submitted moments earlier display \\\"Yesterday\\\" in the employer dashboard. Expected \\\"Today\\\".\", \"evidence\": \"Dashboard: \\\"QA Automation Engineer / Boston, MA · $95k - $130k · Posted Yesterday\\\"; application \\\"Alex Rivera / alex.rivera@example.com / 555-0199 / Yesterday\\\"\"}]}"
